Title: The Confession
Order: 5
Production Code: 1x05

INT. HOSPITAL CORRIDOR - DAY

AMB: distant ward noise

Weeks pass. Dianthe Lusk — an unnamed hospital waif whom no one has recognized — grows stronger under Reuel Briggs's care, though her memory stays a blank. In an unguarded moment, witnessed by Aubrey Livingston, she falls into a standing trance and speaks, unprompted, of "the powers behind the Veil."

DIANTHE LUSK
(trance, eyes closed)
In seven months the sick will be restored. She will wake to worldly cares once more.

Aubrey watches from the doorway, transfixed — and, though pledged to Molly Vance, feels something he shouldn't.

INT. PRIVATE DINING ROOM - NIGHT (CHRISTMAS EVE)

AMB: a fireplace, the clink of coffee cups

Reuel and Aubrey dine alone.

AUBREY LIVINGSTON
There's a link between you and your patient. I felt it the moment she spoke in that trance.

REUEL BRIGGS
(quietly)
I never saw her in the flesh before that night at the Temple, Aubrey. I saw her face first in a storm, alone in my room. Then in the avenue at Hyde House. Call it hallucination if you like — I've decided I don't care. I mean to marry her before her memory ever returns and takes her from me.

AUBREY LIVINGSTON
(significantly)
You forget your own words: "Tramps, stray dogs and Negroes." And your professional career — how can you succeed if it's hinted abroad that you are married to a Negress?

REUEL BRIGGS
I have thought of all that. I will marry her in spite of hell itself.

Aubrey leans across the table, takes his hand, and whispers a single sentence. Reuel starts, and flushes slowly a dark, dull red.

REUEL BRIGGS (CONT'D)
(stammering)
How — where — how did you know it?

AUBREY LIVINGSTON
(quiet, direct)
I have known it since first we met. But the secret is safe with me.
